  "notes": "Mission Bay South Block 12 West, 385 Channel St (1.6 acres) -- the Mission Bay South project area's last remaining undeveloped development parcel (OCII's own Aug 13 2026 Mission Bay CAC presentation: 'Block 12 West last remaining development parcel; no entitlements remain under Mission Bay Plan Documents'). Currently a surface parking lot fronting the China Basin St roundabout; OCII and land owner FOCIL-MB LLC have proposed a Memorandum of Understanding (going to the OCII Commission Sep 2026) to subdivide it into a 1.16-acre, ~265-unit affordable project (up to 90 ft) and a 0.43-acre, ~270-unit market-rate project with an inclusionary requirement (up to 250 ft) -- both preliminary and subject to change, with entitlements (Redevelopment Plan/Design for Development amendments, OPA housing-program amendment, tentative/final subdivision map) still ahead as of this row's sourcing. Classified 'mixed' here (rather than 'residential') because the two halves are two distinct, differently-affordability-restricted projects, not one building.",
